  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c2376a501b724a33beb2889e03cd1418",
      "statement": "HAAPClient.start_friendship drives the full outbound handshake — records the peer locally as pending_out, sends hello with the sender's public key in the payload, replies to the issued challenge with an Ed25519 signature over the challenge ASCII, requires a verify acknowledgement, and finally sends friend_request carrying a capability manifest — over raw endpoint URLs, and the relationship stays pending_out until the remote owner approves and a friend_accept envelope arrives at the requester's server router, which consolidates it via Directory.mark_outbound_accepted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L120-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:acf024697086d9817d04a9e3c66dff66acab8b39b56ab705858e7a3b5ba7af48:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L164-L174",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35536fcd13147b794071a1e310fe567aac600a30cfb45e3da5cb611ccb741f38:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L249-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2feb35fdfa23e46cc7e53ee83b68175299c41141ebe1277965e7373c17e025a6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23d5af1158414f75a398a14ebf793534",
      "statement": "Directory.add_pending_out, used by start_friendship and `haap friends add`, refuses a blocked fingerprint (FriendBlockedError) and a duplicate start against an already-accepted friend (DuplicateRequestError), creates the record with status pending_out, and installs the conservative DEFAULT_GRANT_TEMPLATE (chat:converse, task:delegate, task:submit — never file/exec) unless an explicit matrix is passed, where an explicit {} means deny-everything.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L222-L247",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfc543fe0d265d9f81886ffb9bdf3d8b8191f56362149c67cce3defc1ef6c898:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8bd4de59899a4e77a098f896980155b1",
      "statement": "The server's challenge machinery (hello -> hello_ack -> challenge -> verify) proves private-key possession: _on_hello mints a fresh random 32-byte challenge remembered under the sender's fingerprint with an issue timestamp, and _on_challenge pops that single-use pending challenge (none left raises), enforces 120-second expiry and exact challenge match, verifies the Ed25519 signature over the ASCII challenge against the bootstrap-declared or directory key, registers the sender via register_known (implicit pending_in), and replies verify {verified: True}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L170-L211",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef121eb1b108f25fbfb52a0cedfbdb18de1343e65d5e89a439388c9c3c3d168c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c636a712d43c422bb42ddaf998cda2d3",
      "statement": "Bootstrap messages (hello, challenge, friend_request, and the marketplace service_* types) are verified self-containedly before any handler runs: for an unknown sender the router takes the public key embedded in the payload, requires fingerprint_of_public_key(key) to equal the envelope's sender_fingerprint (else SignatureError/BAD_SIGNATURE), and runs the full envelope verification (±300 s timestamp window, Ed25519 signature, per-sender nonce anti-replay); a non-bootstrap type from an unknown sender is rejected because no key exists to verify it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L240-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1543197e523fc7d85a2c4a30d0eb19acc251b40b00be0bdb27071c3823a3fd7a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L103-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4843543ab98942d5599c5bb526959d134b03cbafef44ffd14b0d0e1dc0e38315:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L131-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be05e4fb1055120deb04e264eb10134991bab4d0811e5df615593421f76d7633:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fff9a20586cb43e0835f098aef1c1a4f",
      "statement": "Server._on_friend_request registers/consolidates the sender, forces the record to pending_in, stores the declared capabilities, and routes to RequestPolicy.evaluate with three reply paths: deny removes the record and answers a signed error envelope with error_code FRIEND_REQUEST_DENIED; auto resolves the capped role template, grants it via directory.approve, and answers friend_accept carrying endpoint, the granted matrix and granted_role; queue keeps the record pending_in, notifies the owner through the Notifier, and answers a friend_request acknowledgement {received: True, pending_human: True, suggested_role, note}. The three paths are audited as friend_request.denied_by_policy, friend_request.auto_approved, and friend_request.queued respectively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L213-L272",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12c4c3a5d1817b629280144ba261141df70433c242b6ad94526240a8219d65f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_812b40c4d6744cc1ad294845dbd07ac4",
      "statement": "Human approval is mandatory in the queue path: pending_in -> accepted happens only through Directory.approve, which is invoked either by the human decision tooling (haap friends approve --role X) or by the server's auto-approve branch of the policy engine — the queue branch only notifies the owner and leaves the record pending_in, so no timer or server path ever self-approves a queued friend request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/cli.py#L105-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6045528f9672a1bb0bdf8a8eebc35e36dd6f995169e9a5b4100afa5790d1823f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L273-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ad92010a5d90f8d0564c16e13a37efaaef9acf13e6c371bcd3d68f8ed8eb2f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L242-L272",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5cdc497edad2363ed737fd2b590e17d25deb5c86d806b64216a267228f4aff74:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d1ed6c5a7f244889695e73b52cee5f1",
      "statement": "RequestPolicy.evaluate decides in a fixed order: deny when the policy default is deny and no auto-approve rule matches; otherwise auto when a rule matches by exact fingerprint or case-insensitive declared speciality (first match wins), with the role taken from the rule or the requested role; otherwise queue as the fallback, whose suggested role equals the requested role capped at max_role. A default: deny policy still auto-approves allowlisted senders.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/policy.py#L81-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5019a3a9381628687fdc2be7c71e1cd22fb6dceda686f81887cedcb0876373a1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3324005c51bd4e60a028d7c03faa497b",
      "statement": "Auto-approval never exceeds max_role: RequestPolicy._cap_role caps a resolved role at the index of max_role on the ladder guest < client < partner < family < admin (default max_role is partner), and a role name not on the ladder — including custom roles.json roles — auto-approves capped at client; the human CLI approval path is not subject to this cap because it resolves the named role directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/cli.py#L105-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6045528f9672a1bb0bdf8a8eebc35e36dd6f995169e9a5b4100afa5790d1823f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/policy.py#L118-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2159fe7742d5654c2843f4566c2a9bbc5aa85600637c84f70495c1028f9daf0a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/policy.py#L48-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e602fd9e6ac7c52cc9207e760c2d60d035f7af21db524601961e75f554fcfed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_383439f550c5407dae463be0077ea1b7",
      "statement": "The friend-request policy is read from $HAAP_DIR/policy.json (structure: default queue|deny, auto_approve rules by fingerprint or speciality with a role, max_role cap); a missing or unreadable/corrupt file falls back to {default: queue, auto_approve: [], max_role: partner}, so the engine's default stance without any configuration is to queue requests for human decision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/policy.py#L47-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9fb1605701da398a3d3ac98d966e6f01ae6e08c2f92b1f46ff85d73b78540a78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c00120d9cc7144368c5a3c317596387e",
      "statement": "Role templates in roles.py bundle a deny-by-default permission matrix plus per-action rate limits: guest (chat/ping only), client (booking scopes booking:*/service:*), partner (task delegation with * scopes plus schedule/calendar reads), family (partner scopes with higher rate limits), admin (adds file:read/write and exec:terminal). Per-instance roles.json entries may extend a built-in via an extends key merged at load time, and resolve_role raises ValueError for unknown role names — the auto-approve branch and the CLI both rely on it to turn one role word into the granted matrix and rate limits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L30-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5a5f0627c68402c82669caf4c80ae4d23419220538dd5861b9331a62c5b2f41:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L8-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2faecc6b52c2ba9942f98ad5ae82493dcb1b24857601e9bb9cbdbb34d0223657:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L98-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7384255573d10cf513d183a4173fc58cd47dfa2a037c1ac082424dbb40072d5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L243-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c68e6d82ba959dc7fe68cf6685c8382bd164b08eb6c4667bc2ad575fc1408813:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c36a62d6f03d4897a388ed2feb726818",
      "statement": "Queued friend requests notify the owner through an injectable Notifier with an actionable card built by policy.build_request (type haap.friend_request, fingerprint, name, truncated message, requested vs suggested role, capabilities, and the exact decision commands how_to_approve = `haap friends approve <fp> --role <suggested_role>` and how_to_deny = `haap friends deny <fp>`); ConsoleNotifier prints the card to stderr, WebhookNotifier POSTs it with an HMAC-SHA256 signature in the X-HAAP-Signature: sha256=... header (targeted at a Hermes owner-chat webhook), CompositeNotifier fans out, and notification failures are swallowed so they never break the protocol.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/policy.py#L134-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a2e6a626d2e530ff4377cbef125b5b722fab2168a09e72bcac86b14cc8b655b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_798af92a12444176852fabf33a4c6332",
      "statement": "friend_accept on the requester side is handled by Server._on_friend_accept, which calls Directory.mark_outbound_accepted: pending_out, pending_in (both sides initiated at once) and already-accepted records all consolidate to accepted idempotently with the peer's declared endpoint merged, while a blocked fingerprint raises FriendBlockedError; the handler replies ping {note: friendship established}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L249-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2feb35fdfa23e46cc7e53ee83b68175299c41141ebe1277965e7373c17e025a6:"
