        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ec7a3c7831d41c28b0806f978b73b6f",
      "statement": "Directory human-decision semantics: register_known records a verified sender and creates an implicit pending_in record only when none exists, never changing an existing relationship's status; approve requires status pending_in and stamps the granted matrix (grant or DEFAULT_GRANT_TEMPLATE) with the note approved by the human owner; deny removes the pending_in record; block marks the fingerprint blocked (creating a tombstone if unknown) and clears permissions to {} so a blocked sender can never act.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L193-L220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a43afa75fbd4b0f81ff03a59499599ceba4af6e9e33d202b77ac3870c57260b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L273-L310",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4142b50194d19b11fc77a7d88291c7f9f67c63bdd3dba100dff5dbef4af1b5c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d35878b5523c459eacb86c6a6e6bdc84",
      "statement": "The friend_accept envelope is the transparent counteroffer: in the auto-approve path the server replies with payload {endpoint: identity.endpoint_url, granted: rec.permissions, granted_role} where granted is the exact matrix installed from the resolved role template; tests assert the granted matrix equals the role template exactly and that the client role grants task:submit but never file:write.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L253-L257",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a610b685c506b4d70a40befdb8302bc08666dafa4f7c0210bb94a2958d8e672:"
        },
        {
